{"book":19,"chapter":12,"rubric":"LINUX NETWORKING / CHAPTER 12","slides":[{"title":"Four stages of the build","sub":"Chapter 12 · Linux networking","short":"Map","main":"A namespace and cable, a bridge, the inner network, the host as router.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["netns+veth","Bridge","Inside","Host"],"captions":["The namespace red and a veth pair: one end inside, the other on the host","The bridge br0 on the host with the gateway address","An address and a default route inside the namespace","ip_forward and NAT address translation on the host"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1. netns red + veth cable","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1. netns red + veth cable","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2. bridge br0 with an address","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1. netns red + veth cable","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2. bridge br0 with an address","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"3. address and route inside","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1. netns red + veth cable","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2. bridge br0 with an address","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"3. address and route inside","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"4. ip_forward + NAT on the host","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.6,21.5,30.4]}]},{"title":"Namespace and cable","sub":"Chapter 12 · Linux networking","short":"veth","main":"A veth pair, moving one end in, the name eth0.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["netns","Pair","Move","lo"],"captions":["ip netns add red creates the namespace","ip link add ... type veth peer name creates a pair of ends","One end moves into red and is named eth0; after the move it is down","The loopback lo inside is down by default, bring it up"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ sudo ip netns add red","$ sudo ip link add vr type veth \\","    peer name vr-br","$ sudo ip link set vr netns red","$ sudo ip -n red link set vr name eth0","$ sudo ip -n red link set lo up"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ sudo ip netns add red","$ sudo ip link add vr type veth \\","    peer name vr-br","$ sudo ip link set vr netns red","$ sudo ip -n red link set vr name eth0","$ sudo ip -n red link set lo up"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ sudo ip netns add red","$ sudo ip link add vr type veth \\","    peer name vr-br","$ sudo ip link set vr netns red","$ sudo ip -n red link set vr name eth0","$ sudo ip -n red link set lo up"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ sudo ip netns add red","$ sudo ip link add vr type veth \\","    peer name vr-br","$ sudo ip link set vr netns red","$ sudo ip -n red link set vr name eth0","$ sudo ip -n red link set lo up"],"hl":[5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[6.6,16.6,28.2]}]},{"title":"A bridge on the host","sub":"Chapter 12 · Linux networking","short":"Bridge","main":"The bridge br0 with the gateway address, the host end as a port.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Bridge","Address","Port","Check"],"captions":["ip link add br0 type bridge creates a switch","The bridge address 10.20